{"title":"1960 AHSME Problems/Problem 21","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1960_AHSME_Problems/Problem_21&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The diagonal of square <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/7/027f4a11d6090f9eac0ce2488df6384dad1263ea.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$I$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/d/add2609af1bb7632cc22b68fd49fdd94de06b327.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a+b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"41\" height=\"16\" />. The perimeter of square <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/f/3/af3906651d16a548230a504127bc5b308a64068f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$II$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" /> with twice the area of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/7/027f4a11d6090f9eac0ce2488df6384dad1263ea.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$I$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> is:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/7/6/476a1c094bcd7d9f09140c25f6e56240abd667e7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ (a+b)^2\\qquad \\textbf{(B)}\\ \\sqrt{2}(a+b)^2\\qquad \\textbf{(C)}\\ 2(a+b)\\qquad \\textbf{(D)}\\ \\sqrt{8}(a+b) \\qquad \\textbf{(E)}\\ 4(a+b)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"653\" height=\"21\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1960_AHSME_Problems/Problem_21&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Since the diagonal of square <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/7/027f4a11d6090f9eac0ce2488df6384dad1263ea.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$I$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/d/add2609af1bb7632cc22b68fd49fdd94de06b327.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a+b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"41\" height=\"16\" /> units long, the side length of square <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/7/027f4a11d6090f9eac0ce2488df6384dad1263ea.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$I$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/6/b/46bdb7f753b22e68b227fe374b2a1ccdf2da80e3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{a+b}{\\sqrt{2}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"42\" height=\"42\" />, so the area of square <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/7/027f4a11d6090f9eac0ce2488df6384dad1263ea.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$I$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/4/c/a4c65e50915d4cc422cc62c073b15de7e6e3885e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{(a+b)^2}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"67\" height=\"41\" />.\n</p><p>The area of square <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/f/3/af3906651d16a548230a504127bc5b308a64068f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$II$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" /> is twice as much as the area of square <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/7/027f4a11d6090f9eac0ce2488df6384dad1263ea.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$I$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, so the area of square <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/f/3/af3906651d16a548230a504127bc5b308a64068f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$II$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/6/d/66da20c7db80f65c8d9bc915822a6e5df66bfb3e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a+b)^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"60\" height=\"19\" />.  That means the side length of square <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/f/3/af3906651d16a548230a504127bc5b308a64068f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$II$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/d/add2609af1bb7632cc22b68fd49fdd94de06b327.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a+b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"41\" height=\"16\" />, so the perimeter of square <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/f/3/af3906651d16a548230a504127bc5b308a64068f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$II$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/8/4/c84cd0ef6a19c9f7bfdf8cca4feb186f410cd204.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4(a+b)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" />, or answer choice <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/b/f/6bfc0829f3f29bbf35d0a861644e00cfef0f50ca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(E)}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"39\" height=\"28\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1960_AHSME_Problems/Problem_21&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1960_AHSME\" title=\"1960 AHSME\">1960 AHSC</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1960_AHSME_Problems\" title=\"1960 AHSME Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1960_AHSME_Answer_Key\" title=\"1960 AHSME Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\